_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened a pull request against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That made 2.665 round to 2.67 when the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so the fix follows the test and the code's docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}